          "explanation": ""
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "$84$",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "index": 2,
          "imageUrl": "",
          "explanation": ""
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "$93$",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "index": 3,
          "imageUrl": "",
          "explanation": ""
        }
      ],
      "answer": "",
      "alternateAnswers": [],
      "explanation": "Let the tens digit be $x$ and the units digit be $y$. The original number is $10x + y$. The reversed number is $10y + x$. We are given $x + y = 12$ and $(10y + x) - (10x + y) = 54 \\implies 9y - 9x = 54 \\implies y - x = 6$. Adding the equations $x + y = 12$ and $-x + y = 6$, we get $2y = 18 \\implies y = 9$. Substituting $y = 9$, we get $x = 3$. The original number is $39$.",
