      "explanation": "When compounded half-yearly, the rate is halved and the time is doubled. $P = ₹10,000$. Rate ($R$) $= \\frac{10\\%}{2} = 5\\%$ per half-year. Time ($n$) $= 1.5 \\text{ years} \\times 2 = 3$ half-years. Amount $A = P \\left(1 + \\frac{R}{100}\\right)^n = 10000 \\left(1 + \\frac{5}{100}\\right)^3 = 10000 \\left(\\frac{21}{20}\\right)^3 = 10000 \\times \\frac{9261}{8000} = \\frac{92610}{8} = ₹11576.25$. Compound Interest $= A - P = 11576.25 - 10000 = ₹1576.25$.",
